-- Adversarial saturation stress (META_STRESS theory #5). Forward `@auto`
-- rules that regenerate each other's output under genuine pressure, written to
-- exercise the two saturation guards independently: the *recipe* dedupe key
-- (rule + source tuple) and the *canonical surface shape* key (metas numbered
-- by first occurrence). Every probe goal `R` is unprovable, so each theorem is
-- a no-result probe: the saturation must stay bounded, report exhaustion
-- honestly, and never invent a suggestion.
--
-- The predicate families are disjoint so each loop class fires in isolation
-- (`comm` only sees `P`, `ping`/`pong` only `S`/`T`, `viaA`/`viaB` only
-- `A`/`B`), letting the per-probe derived-ref counts pin down dedupe behavior.
delimiter $ ( ) $;
provable sort wff;
sort obj;

term P (x: obj): wff;
term S (x: obj): wff;
term T (x: obj): wff;
term A (x: obj): wff;
term B (x: obj): wff;
term C (x: obj): wff;

term g (x y: obj): obj;
term h (x: obj): obj;
term K1: obj;
term K2: obj;
term R: wff;

-- Commutativity loop: swapping the arguments regenerates from the rule's own
-- output. `P (g K1 K2)` derives `P (g K2 K1)` (a NEW surface shape, so it is
-- kept), but re-firing on that derived fact yields `P (g K1 K2)` again, whose
-- shape is already seen and dropped. The recipe key keeps the rule from
-- re-firing on a source it already consumed. Together they must close the loop
-- at a fixpoint (exhausted = false), NOT spin to the layer/fact budget.
--| @auto forward
axiom comm (x y: obj): $ P (g x y) $ > $ P (g y x) $;

-- Mutual regeneration: `ping`/`pong` build an ever-deeper `h`-tower
-- (`S K1` -> `T (h K1)` -> `S (h (h K1))` -> ...). Genuinely unbounded, so the
-- frontier stays productive at every layer and the run must stop on the budget
-- with exhaustion reported (exhausted = true).
--| @auto forward
axiom ping (x: obj): $ S x $ > $ T (h x) $;
--| @auto forward
axiom pong (x: obj): $ T x $ > $ S (h x) $;

-- Confluence: two distinct recipes derive the identical fact `C K1`. The
-- recipe keys differ (different rule + source), so the surface shape key is
-- what must collapse them to a single derived ref.
--| @auto forward
axiom viaA (x: obj): $ A x $ > $ C x $;
--| @auto forward
axiom viaB (x: obj): $ B x $ > $ C x $;

theorem comm_loop: $ P (g K1 K2) $ > $ R $;
theorem mutual_regen: $ S K1 $ > $ R $;
theorem confluence: $ A K1 $ > $ B K1 $ > $ R $;
